[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Mud is Mud]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.27]Lesson 52 | 第52课
[00:02.21]Mud is mud | 泥就是泥
[00:10.04]Why did Harry decide to give up his little game? | 哈里为什么决定放弃他的小游戏？
[00:15.35]My cousin, Harry, keeps a large curiously-shaped bottle on permanent display in his study. | 我的堂兄哈里在他的书房里一直摆着一只形状古怪的大瓶子。
[00:23.47]Despite the fact that the bottle is tinted a delicate shade of green, | 尽管那只瓶子呈淡绿色，
[00:27.74]an observant visitor would soon notice that it is filled with what looks like a thick, greyish substance. | 但细心的客人很快就会注意到瓶子里装的是一种看上去像黏稠的灰色的东西。
[00:35.60]If you were to ask Harry what was in the bottle, he would tell you that it contained perfumed mud. | 如果你问哈里瓶子里是什么，他会告诉你里面装的是香水泥。
[00:42.44]If you expressed doubt or surprise, he would immediately invite you to smell it and then to rub some into your skin. | 如果你表示怀疑或惊讶，他会立刻请你去闻一闻，然后取一些抹在皮肤上。
[00:52.01]The brief experiment would dispel any further doubts she might have. | 这个简单的实验会消除她可能还存有的任何疑虑。
[00:56.84]The bottle really does contain perfumed mud. | 瓶子里装的确实是香水泥。
[01:00.80]How Harry came into the possession of this outlandish stuff makes an interesting story which he is fond of relating. | 哈里是如何得到这件稀奇古怪的东西的，本身就是一个有趣的故事，而且他爱讲这个故事。
[01:09.36]Furthermore, the acquisition of this bottle cured him of a bad habit he had been developing for years. | 此外，获得这只瓶子还治好了他多年养成的一个坏习惯。
[01:17.66]Harry used to consider it a great joke to go into expensive cosmetic shops and make outrageous requests for goods that do not exist. | 哈里过去常认为，跑进名贵化妆品商店，荒唐地索要一些根本不存在的商品是个极大的乐趣。
[01:28.92]He would invent fanciful names on the spot. | 他会当场编造出稀奇古怪的商品名称。
[01:32.37]On entering a shop, | 一进商店，
[01:34.06]he would ask for a new perfume called 'Scented Shadow' or for 'insoluble bath cubes'. | 他就提出要一种名叫“影子香”的新香水，或者要“不溶性浴片”。
[01:42.32]If a shop assistant told him she had not heard of it, he would pretend to be considerably put out. | 如果售货员告诉他从未听说过这些东西，他就会假装大为不悦。
[01:49.63]He loved to be told that one of his imaginary products was temporarily out of stock | 他喜欢听到人家说他虚构的产品暂时脱销，
[01:56.35]and he would faithfully promise to call again at some future date, but of course he never did. | 然后就会信誓旦旦地保证改天再来买。当然，他从未再来过。
[02:03.27]How Harry managed to keep a straight face during these performances is quite beyond me. | 哈里在这些表演中怎么能始终板着脸，这我实在弄不明白。
[02:10.31]Harry does not need to be prompted to explain how he bought his precious bottle of mud. | 哈里无需人请求就会解释他是如何买到他那瓶珍贵的泥巴的。
[02:16.10]One day, he went to an exclusive shop in London and asked for 'Myrolite'. | 一天，他去伦敦一家高档商店，提出要买“迈罗利特”。
[02:23.14]The shop assistant looked puzzled and Harry repeated the word, slowly stressing each syllable. | 售货员满脸疑惑，哈里又慢慢地重复了一遍这个词，一字一顿。
[02:31.00]When the woman shook her head in bewilderment, | 当那位女售货员困惑地摇了摇头时，
[02:34.19]Harry went on to explain that 'myrolite' was a hard, amber-like substance which could be used to remove freckles. | 哈里又解释说，“迈罗利特”是一种坚硬的、琥珀色的物质，可以用来除去雀斑。
[02:44.08]This explanation evidently conveyed something to the woman who searched shelf after shelf. | 这番解释显然让那位女售货员领悟了些什么，她把一个又一个货架都找遍了。
[02:50.69]She produced all sorts of weird concoctions, but none of them met with Harry's requirements. | 她拿出各种稀奇古怪的化妆品，但没有一样符合哈里的要求。
[02:58.09]When Harry put on his act of being mildly annoyed, the assistant promised to order some for him. | 当哈里装出有些生气的样子时，售货员答应为他订购一些。
[03:05.09]Intoxicated by his success, Harry then asked for perfumed mud. | 哈里被自己的成功所陶醉，接着又提出要买香水泥。
[03:11.64]He expected the assistant to look at him in blank astonishment. | 他原以为售货员会茫然惊讶地望着他。
[03:15.81]However, it was his turn to be surprised, for the woman's eyes immediately lit up | 然而这一回惊讶的却是他自己了，因为那位女售货员的眼睛顿时亮了起来，
[03:23.01]and she fetched several bottles which she placed on the counter for Harry to inspect. | 她取来了好几瓶摆在柜台上供哈里挑选。
[03:29.03]For once, Harry had to admit defeat. | 这一次，哈里只好认输了。
[03:32.65]He picked up what seemed to be the smallest bottle and discreetly asked the price. | 他拿起看上去最小的一瓶，谨慎地问了价钱。
[03:39.30]He was glad to get away with a mere twenty pounds and he beat a hasty retreat, clutching the precious bottle under his arm. | 他庆幸自己只花了区区20英镑就得以脱身。他把那只宝贵的瓶子夹在腋下，仓皇溜走了。
[03:48.57]From then on, Harry decided that this little game he had invented might prove to be expensive. | 从那以后，哈里认定自己发明的这个小游戏可能代价高昂。
[03:55.68]The curious bottle which now adorns the bookcase in his study was his first and last purchase of rare cosmetics. | 如今摆在他书房书架上装饰的那只古怪的瓶子，是他头一次也是最后一次购买稀有化妆品。
